  "_notes": [
    "\uD83D\uDEA9 unitPrice.gross EQUALS the line's unitPrice.gross for the same item under the same header — the whole ticket (875 / §3.4 rule 1). The two are one engine run at one header: the ORDER's plant, the C000 seat, its loyalty and its Z00001 procedure, at qty 1.",
    "It is VAT-INCLUSIVE. The search row's estimatePriceExVat is Item.UnitPrice, a material-master column BEFORE the separate 15% MWST condition, so it reads ~13% under what the caller pays. On a search row a real line contradicts it seconds later; a price check is read out loud with nothing beside it, which is why a pricing failure here is a typed refusal and never a fallback to that number.",
    "\uD83D\uDEA9 IT TAKES NO CLAIM. Captured under a live 15-second strict lease held by the agent's own register: the price check answers, and getState — which resumes — answers SESSION_BUSY on the same lease. That is why 'how much is that?' never pauses order entry.",
    "offersComplete is FALSE and will stay false until 787-C lands (130: BBY lookup keys on the condition-side access tables, so a one-item run never loads a 'buy X get Y' whose X is the priced item). It flips to true with NO client change.",
    "The client sends transactionId and itemNumber and NOTHING else — no quantity (always one unit, owner ruling), no plant, no sales org, no condition. This is deliberately NOT Pricing/Simulate, whose body carries manual conditions and a sales org that would beat the plant's, and whose grant is the pricing-analysis screen's."
  ]
}
